fullDescription.text:
Reports declarations of procedures and functions that are missing their implementation in code. In Oracle, you can declare a procedure or a function without its body, and write the implementation later. The inspection will report names of such procedures or functions that are left without implementation. Example (Oracle): 'DECLARE PROCEDURE foo(a int, b varchar2);
BEGIN
    NULL;
END;' The 'foo' procedure is declared but is missing implementation. We can add the implementation to get rid of the error. 'DECLARE PROCEDURE foo(a int, b varchar2);
  PROCEDURE foo(a int, b varchar2) IS
BEGIN
    NULL;
END;
BEGIN
    NULL;
END;'

fullDescription.markdown:
Reports declarations of procedures and functions that are missing their implementation in code.

In Oracle, you can declare a procedure or a function without its body, and write the implementation later. The inspection will report names
of such procedures or functions that are left without implementation.

Example (Oracle):

    DECLARE PROCEDURE foo(a int, b varchar2);
    BEGIN
        NULL;
    END;

The `foo` procedure is declared but is missing implementation. We can add the implementation to get rid of the error.

    DECLARE PROCEDURE foo(a int, b varchar2);
      PROCEDURE foo(a int, b varchar2) IS
    BEGIN
        NULL;
    END;
    BEGIN
        NULL;
    END;

